--TEST--
text pulled out of `mixed` is `tainted` in every form, so a request value reaches a query only after it is checked, and a shape or a binding that receives it must be written `tainted` — `rule:security/taint-propagation`, `rule:security/tainted-sources`, `rule:types/type-test`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The accepted half is
// tests/conformance/lang/mixed-text-converts-to-the-tainted-form-and-a-number-stays-clean.nvst.
var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

// The two ways a request body's value reached a query as plain text.
$db->query("select * from users where id = " . Core\Request::json(), []);
string $id = Core\Request::json() as string;

// Each other way text leaves `mixed`, bound at the plain type.
mixed $m = Core\Json::decode('"x"');
?string $n = $m as ?string;
bytes $b = $m as bytes;
array<string> $list = $m as array<string>;
secret string $k = $m as secret string;
string $inter = "id {$m}";
if ($m is string) {
    string $narrowed = $m;
}

// A written shape or binding says `tainted` itself, from `mixed` and from `object`.
echo ($m as {name: string})->name, "\n";
if ($m is {name: string}) {
    echo "tested\n";
}
object $o = {name: "x"};
echo ($o as {name: string})->name, "\n";
foreach ($m as string $v) {
    echo $v;
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]

[db.main]
driver = "sqlite"
path = ":memory:"
--EXPECT--

